{"title":"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A company sells rectangular business cards. Each card has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/3/773364718d825a37e31cda99985c2e0ca46e0730.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ cm} \\times 9 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />. Cards are printed on a page and then the page is cut to produce the individual cards.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the area of each business card in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/e/cce95ec3eb5f2ff5452281e5b03c39757b163de2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cm}^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"17\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the dimensions of each business card, the width is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/b/edb6c124e4e493c37260e6af2f2d74ee0099439d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> and the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/2/502589758507658a9cbe6da079e1bd5a817de861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\text { cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Using the formula for the area of a rectangle, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234df48612b573a447f2b39796a318edce3d85be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = 5 \\text { cm} \\times 9 \\text { cm} = \\boxed{45 \\text{ cm}^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"222\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018014430\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.008 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 27/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 988/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.208      1 2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%    6.208      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35541:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018014430 and revision id 277868. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}